userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: A slow neutron absorbed by uranium-235 forms an unstable U-236 compound nucleus that deforms and splits into Ba-141 and Kr-92 plus three neutrons and a large burst of energy — and those three neutrons can trigger further fissions, sustaining a chain reaction.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Fission consumes one neutron but emits three — that surplus is what turns a single nuclear event into an exponentially growing chain reaction.
DEMO STEPS: 7 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
{
  "concept": "A slow neutron absorbed by uranium-235 forms an unstable U-236 compound nucleus that deforms and splits into Ba-141 and Kr-92 plus three neutrons and a large burst of energy — and those three neutrons can trigger further fissions, sustaining a chain reaction.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Incoming neutron: small mid-grey shaded sphere at far left, labeled in isotope notation (superscript 1, subscript 0, n)",
    "Black arrow from the incoming neutron toward the U-235 nucleus, with short pale impact streaks drawn only at the moment of contact",
    "U-235 nucleus: large space-filling cluster of interlocking medium-green spheres (protons) and mid-grey spheres (neutrons), label '235 over 92, U' set clearly below and clear of the cluster outline",
    "Black arrow from U-235 to the intermediate nucleus",
    "U-236 compound nucleus: same green/grey packing, first drawn as a slightly larger sphere, then as an elongated pinched dumbbell, thin dark-red contour, labels '236 over 92, U' and 'Unstable nucleus' placed well below the shape",
    "Two black arrows fanning up-right and down-right from the scission point to the two daughter nuclei",
    "Kr-92 daughter nucleus: smaller green/grey cluster upper right, label '92 over 36, Kr' offset outward (up-right) away from the cluster edge",
